{"text":"kuruntokai","n":137,"lines":["மெல்லியல் அரிவைநின் னல்லகம் புலம்ப","நிற்றுறந் தமைகுவெ னாயின் எற்றுறந்","திரவலர் வாரா வைகல்","பலவா குகயான் செலவுறு தகவே"],"tr":["melliyal arivainiṉ ṉallakam pulampa","niṟṟuṟan tamaikuve ṉāyiṉ eṟṟuṟan","tiravalar vārā vaikal","palavā kukayāṉ celavuṟu takavē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"pālai","tinai_ta":"பாலை","speaker_ta":"தலைவன் கூற்று","poet_ta":"பாலை பாடிய பெருங் கடுங்கோ","speaker_en":"the hero (talaivaṉ)","poet_tr":"Pālai Pāṭiya Peruṅ Kaṭuṅkō"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 14, veṇcīr 1"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 8, veṇṭaḷai 6"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"மெல்லியல்","tr":"melliyal","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"மெல்","tr":"mel"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"லியல்","tr":"liyal"}]},{"text":"அரிவைநின்","tr":"arivainiṉ","foot":"puḷimāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"அரி","tr":"ari"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வை","tr":"vai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"நின்","tr":"niṉ"}]},{"text":"னல்லகம்","tr":"ṉallakam","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"னல்","tr":"ṉal"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"லகம்","tr":"lakam"}]},{"text":"புலம்ப","tr":"pulampa","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"புலம்","tr":"pulam"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ப","tr":"pa"}]}],[{"text":"நிற்றுறந்","tr":"niṟṟuṟan","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"நிற்","tr":"niṟ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"றுறந்","tr":"ṟuṟan"}]},{"text":"தமைகுவெ","tr":"tamaikuve","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"தமை","tr":"tamai"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"குவெ","tr":"kuve"}]},{"text":"னாயின்","tr":"ṉāyiṉ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"னா","tr":"ṉā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யின்","tr":"yiṉ"}]},{"text":"எற்றுறந்","tr":"eṟṟuṟan","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"எற்","tr":"eṟ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"றுறந்","tr":"ṟuṟan"}]}],[{"text":"திரவலர்","tr":"tiravalar","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"திர","tr":"tira"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"வலர்","tr":"valar"}]},{"text":"வாரா","tr":"vārā","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வா","tr":"vā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ரா","tr":"rā"}]},{"text":"வைகல்","tr":"vaikal","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வை","tr":"vai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கல்","tr":"kal"}]}],[{"text":"பலவா","tr":"palavā","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பல","tr":"pala"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வா","tr":"vā"}]},{"text":"குகயான்","tr":"kukayāṉ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குக","tr":"kuka"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யான்","tr":"yāṉ"}]},{"text":"செலவுறு","tr":"celavuṟu","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"செல","tr":"cela"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"வுறு","tr":"vuṟu"}]},{"text":"தகவே","tr":"takavē","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"தக","tr":"taka"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வே","tr":"vē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"மெல்லியல்","parts":[{"text":"மெல்","lemma":"மெல்","gloss":"soft"},{"text":"இயல்","lemma":"இயல்","gloss":"nature"}],"gloss":"soft-natured"},{"surface":"அரிவை","parts":[{"text":"அரிவை","lemma":"அரிவை","gloss":"young woman"}],"gloss":"young woman"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"நல்","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good"},{"surface":"அகம்","parts":[{"text":"அகம்","lemma":"அகம்","gloss":"heart"}],"gloss":"heart"},{"surface":"புலம்ப","parts":[{"text":"புலம்ப","lemma":"புலம்பு","gloss":"to suffer"}],"gloss":"to suffer"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நிற்றுறந்","parts":[{"text":"நிற்றுறந்","lemma":"நிற்றுறந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தமைகுவெ","parts":[{"text":"தமைகுவெ","lemma":"தமைகுவெ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"னாயின்","parts":[{"text":"னாயின்","lemma":"னாயின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எற்றுறந்","parts":[{"text":"எற்றுறந்","lemma":"எற்றுறந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"திரவலர்","parts":[{"text":"திரவலர்","lemma":"திரவலர்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வாரா","parts":[{"text":"வாரா","lemma":"வாரா","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வைகல்","parts":[{"text":"வைகல்","lemma":"வைகல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"பல","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many"},{"surface":"ஆகுக","parts":[{"text":"ஆகுக","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"may they become"}],"gloss":"may they become"},{"surface":"யான்","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I"},{"surface":"செலவு","parts":[{"text":"செலவு","lemma":"செலவு","gloss":"journey"}],"gloss":"journey"},{"surface":"உறு","parts":[{"text":"உறு","lemma":"உறு","gloss":"undertaking"}],"gloss":"undertaking"},{"surface":"தகவே","parts":[{"text":"தகவு","lemma":"தகவு","gloss":"fitness"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"fitness indeed"}]}],"literal":"Soft-natured young woman, your good heart suffering, / if I agree to abandon you, having abandoned me, / days when suppliants do not come / may they become many, indeed, the fitness of my undertaking the journey.","translation":"O soft-natured young woman! If I can tolerate abandoning you, leaving your good heart to suffer in loneliness, then let the days when suppliants abandon me and do not come to seek charity become many. That indeed would be the fitting consequence of my undertaking this journey.","modern":"மென்மையான இயல்புடைய பெண்ணே! உன்னுடைய நல்ல நெஞ்சம் வருந்துமாறு உன்னைத் பிரிந்து செல்ல நான் உடன்படுவேனானால், என்னை விடுத்து இரவலர்கள் வராத நாட்கள் பலவாகட்டும்; அதுவே நான் மேற்கொள்ளும் இப்பயணத்திற்குத் தகுந்த பயனாகும்.","explanation":"The speaker is the hero, who is contemplating a journey through the arid wasteland to acquire wealth. He addresses his beloved, a soft-natured young woman, acknowledging that his departure would leave her good heart in deep loneliness and grief. He makes a solemn vow: if he is cold-hearted enough to leave her suffering just to seek wealth, let him be cursed with the worst fate for a generous householder—that suppliants abandon him and no one comes to seek charity. In classical Tamil culture, earning wealth is meant for sharing with others; thus, a journey that destroys love and fails to enable charity is completely worthless. Through this powerful oath, he expresses his deep love and implies that he cannot bear to leave her.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.2],[1.3,1.7],[1.7,1.9],[1.9,2.4],[2.4,2.65],[2.65,2.65],[2.65,2.65],[2.65,2.9],[2.9,3.42],[3.42,6.0],[6.0,6.92],[6.92,7.55],[7.55,7.67],[7.67,7.97]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.5],[1.57,1.9],[1.9,2.1],[3.04,4.45],[4.92,5.86],[5.86,6.33],[6.33,6.33],[6.33,6.33],[6.33,6.33],[6.33,6.8],[6.8,7.74],[7.74,8.42],[8.42,8.56],[8.56,8.86]]}}